From fc04e0b8bc2b98aea134fabd095360cc6c8de926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:34:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] Web client (S1): a caravan's arrival in five states,
 from the records and the program's rules; 04's and 05's sources
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

hud/statussources.mjs says where each state comes from. A caravan's arrival
is told in five states and never as "arrived" when that is not known:
- past its arrival turn and still on the road: overdue, not concluded (the
  S1 village card no longer says 到着済み for it)
- CARAVAN_SETTLED with outcome lost: lost, final
- delivered to a storehouse: not verified. settle_caravan cuts each amount
  at the vault's cap while the record keeps the whole cargo.
- delivered to a village: Holding::credit adds the whole cargo with no cap,
  so it is verified full or partial against CARAVAN_SENT's cargo (which is
  after the towers' wear). It stays not verified when that send was not read.
statusview.mjs's arrival contract becomes these five states; 0004's three
("unverified", "partial", "full") are gone. 04's own arrival, 04's cancel
of a caravan, 05's costs of a village and 05's switch back to manual play
come from sources their owners register. With none registered, nothing of
theirs is shown. Needs 0003 and 0004 (updates 0004's test; 0005's screen harness is updated by 0007).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
